  "about": "What a desktop's QR code carries (lazysend://pair?...) and what a reader must make of it. result is ok, notPairingCode, newerVersion or damaged. For ok, pairing holds what is read; checkCode is the six digits the two screens show, from the first 4 bytes of the fingerprint, spaced 3 and 3. The fingerprint is the bytes 0 to 31, the token the bytes 16 to 31.",
